note.text:
Reagent bottles carry hazard symbols (red diamonds) that warn of danger:
• a flame: flammable, catches fire easily (ethanol, kerosene);
• a flame over a circle: oxidising, makes other things burn fiercely (potassium manganate(VII));
• a skull and crossbones: toxic, poisonous (mercury);
• liquid dripping onto a hand and metal: corrosive, destroys skin and metal (concentrated acids, sodium hydroxide);
• an exclamation mark: harmful or irritant;
• an exploding bomb: explosive;
• a dead tree and fish: dangerous for the environment.
Read the label before you open a bottle, and never mix chemicals without the teacher's instruction.
